P5-AD-followup — advisory citations side-finding:
  Origin: post-deploy walk on 2026-05-19. `domains: ["cpf"]` was correct
  but `provisions_cited` came back empty in conversation history because
  the prod KB stores Domain rows as sub-areas ("CPF Contribution Rates"
  etc.), not "cpf". The engine pre-seed's
  `_kb_search_provisions(domain="cpf")` matched 0 rows.

  Fix:
  - NEW src/hr_advisory/kb/domain_lookup.py — lifts the domain → Act.short_name
    mapping out of compliance.py. Exposes provisions_for_domain(),
    normalize_domain_key(), get_act_short_names(), DOMAIN_ALIASES.
  - advisory_engine.py pre-seed now routes through provisions_for_domain
    (Act-based lookup) — the same model the compliance check uses.
  - Pre-seed format string reads from provision-row fields (section,
    title, plain_summary, formal_text), not the search_kb wrapper output.
  - Classifier renamed: efma → foreign_manpower, tafep → fair_employment,
    tax_iras → tax. Legacy spellings accepted via DOMAIN_ALIASES.
  - compliance.py refactored to use the shared module (DRY).

P5-DM-2 shifts seed (via UI walkthrough on prod):
  - 3 shift templates created: Morning (08:00-16:00), Afternoon
    (14:00-22:00), Night (22:00-06:00)
  - 22 assignments populating Mon-Fri of the week of 2026-05-18:
    2 Morning + 2 Afternoon staff daily + Muhammad Rizwan on Night Tue+Thu
  - Week officially published (ShiftPublish row id=2)
  - This is prod-data work, not a code change. P5-DM-1 (payroll variance)
    stays blocked by P4-XX-2 Xero schema deferral.

P5-DM-2 publish-toast UX fix:
  apps/web/src/app/(dashboard)/shifts/page.tsx:
    The Publish Week button worked silently — no toast, no state change.
    The user couldn't tell their click did anything and would re-click,
    creating duplicate ShiftPublish audit rows.
    Fix: toast.success on happy path, toast.error on failure,
    isPublishing state guards double-clicks (button disables +
    label flips to "Publishing…"). Pinned via 4 new regression tests.

